## Example answer

You can use the low-level capture API rather than an `AudioCaptureComponent`. The exact header and parameter names can vary between UE5 versions, so check the `IAudioCapture` declaration in your engine installation if a signature differs. The important parts are to open the stream with a callback, start it, and stop and close it when finished.

```cpp
// MyGameMode.h
#pragma once

#include "CoreMinimal.h"
#include "GameFramework/GameModeBase.h"
#include "MyGameMode.generated.h"

class IAudioCapture;

UCLASS()
class YOURGAME_API AMyGameMode : public AGameModeBase
{
    GENERATED_BODY()

public:
    virtual void BeginPlay() override;
    virtual void EndPlay(const EEndPlayReason::Type EndPlayReason) override;

private:
    TSharedPtr<IAudioCapture> Capture;
};
```

```cpp
// MyGameMode.cpp
#include "MyGameMode.h"
#include "AudioCapture.h"
#include "Interfaces/IAudioCapture.h"

void AMyGameMode::BeginPlay()
{
    Super::BeginPlay();

    Capture = FAudioCapture::Create();
    if (!Capture.IsValid())
    {
        UE_LOG(LogTemp, Error, TEXT("Could not create audio capture device."));
        return;
    }

    IAudioCapture::FCaptureParams Params;
    Params.DeviceIndex = INDEX_NONE; // Default input device
    Params.SampleRate = 48000;
    Params.NumChannels = 1;
    Params.Callback = [this](
        const void* AudioData,
        int32 NumFrames,
        int32 NumChannels,
        int32 SampleRate,
        double StreamTime,
        bool bOverflow)
    {
        // This callback runs on the audio-capture thread.
        // Copy the data here if it must be processed on the game thread.
        // Avoid doing expensive work or calling most UObject APIs here.
    };

    if (!Capture->OpenStream(Params))
    {
        UE_LOG(LogTemp, Error, TEXT("Could not open audio capture stream."));
        Capture.Reset();
        return;
    }

    if (!Capture->StartStream())
    {
        UE_LOG(LogTemp, Error, TEXT("Could not start audio capture stream."));
        Capture->CloseStream();
        Capture.Reset();
    }
}

void AMyGameMode::EndPlay(const EEndPlayReason::Type EndPlayReason)
{
    if (Capture.IsValid())
    {
        Capture->StopStream();
        Capture->CloseStream();
        Capture.Reset();
    }

    Super::EndPlay(EndPlayReason);
}
```

Enable the Audio Capture plugin and add its relevant module—typically `AudioCaptureCore` for this low-level API—to your `.Build.cs` dependencies. Also note that `AGameMode` exists on the server, not on every client. For a client’s microphone, a local-player-owned class is generally a better place to start and manage capture.

