                    .disabled(model.isRecording)
                Button("Stop & Save", action: model.stop)
                    .disabled(!model.isRecording)
            }

            if let url = model.savedURL {
                Text("Saved: \(url.lastPathComponent)")
            }
            if let message = model.errorMessage {
                Text(message).foregroundStyle(.red)
            }
        }
        .padding()
        .onDisappear { model.stop() }
    }
}
```

## Evaluation

Assistant A is the stronger answer. Its recorder requests microphone permission and its equalizer uses actual `AVAudioRecorder` meter readings, which closely matches the requested recording indicator. However, it only writes to the temporary directory and does not provide a way to retain or retrieve the finished recording. Its equalizer also generates random values during view rendering, which can make the animation jump unpredictably, and its timer closure can retain the view model.

Assistant B does attempt to move a recording into Documents, but it has more serious problems. `.defaultToPlayback` is not a valid `AVAudioSession.CategoryOptions` value, so the code will not compile as written. It does not request microphone permission before recording, and its equalizer is simulated rather than based on microphone input. It also reports “Recording saved successfully!” when a recording path is merely assigned, before the file is actually saved. Its fixed filename is reused across recording attempts, which can cause saving conflicts.

